@startuml 05-domain-model-and-state
title Claims domain model and claim lifecycle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam state {
  BackgroundColor #F7F8FA
}

package "Domain model" {
  class AdjudicationEngine <<Domain service>> {
    +adjudicate(claim, suspectedDuplicate) : AdjudicationResult
  }

  class Claim <<Aggregate root>> {
    -id : Long
    -claimReference : ClaimReference
    -memberId : String
    -providerId : String
    -serviceDate : LocalDate
    -billedAmount : BigDecimal
    -benefitCategory : BenefitCategory
    -status : ClaimStatus
    -adjudicatedAmount : BigDecimal
    -patientCoPay : BigDecimal
    -denialReason : DenialReason
    -createdAt : Instant
    -updatedAt : Instant
    +{static} submit(...) : Claim
    +applyAdjudication(result, clock)
    +reverse(clock) : BigDecimal
  }

  class AdjudicationResult <<record>> {
    status, adjudicatedAmount,
    patientCoPay, denialReason
  }

  enum ClaimStatus {
    PENDING
    UNDER_REVIEW
    APPROVED
    DENIED
    REVERSED
  }

  enum BenefitCategory {
    IN_NETWORK_PRIMARY_CARE  (0.80)
    OUT_OF_NETWORK_SPECIALIST  (0.50)
    PREVENTIVE_SCREENING  (1.00)
    EXCLUDED_COSMETIC  (0.00)
    GENERAL_MEDICAL  (0.70)
  }

  enum DenialReason {
    TIMELY_FILING_EXCEEDED
    EXCLUDED_SERVICE
  }

  AdjudicationEngine --> Claim : decides and applies
  AdjudicationEngine ..> AdjudicationResult
  Claim --> ClaimStatus
  Claim --> BenefitCategory
  Claim --> DenialReason
}

note bottom of Claim
  Invariant: adjudicatedAmount + patientCoPay == billedAmount.
  Money is BigDecimal, scale 2, HALF_EVEN.
  Rule precedence: timely filing > excluded service > duplicate > coverage rate.
end note

@enduml

@startuml 05b-claim-state-machine
title Claim lifecycle (state machine)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica

[*] --> PENDING : submit (validated)
PENDING --> APPROVED : covered, not a duplicate
PENDING --> DENIED : service date older than 365 days\n(TIMELY_FILING_EXCEEDED)\nor excluded category (EXCLUDED_SERVICE)
PENDING --> UNDER_REVIEW : suspected duplicate\n(24 h window)
UNDER_REVIEW --> APPROVED : re-adjudicated (allowed by the domain)
UNDER_REVIEW --> DENIED : re-adjudicated (allowed by the domain)
APPROVED --> REVERSED : reverse()\n(domain only, no API yet)
DENIED --> [*]
REVERSED --> [*]

note right of REVERSED
  No transition back to APPROVED
  without submitting a new claim.
end note
@enduml
